A||||8||Gold-86SE||Another One Bites the Dust||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||02-28-2001||10:26 AM||||<BR>And another one's gone,<BR>And another one's gone.<BR>Another one bites the dust.<BR>Hey, hey<P>A little Queen there.<P>Allow me to use to bandwidth to relay my experience from last evening.<P>Ok, I am going back home.  I am trying to get around someone and they speed up on me, so I speed up to 80 and bam, I lose power, feels just like a governor shut down when the maximum speed is reached. I thinking to myself, "did I lose my tranny? fourth gear? what's going on?"<P>So, I slow down, again thinking to myself, "I need to get off the freeway, so I can limp it home in third gear." I take the next exit, and have it in 3rd, and still losing power, so I push down the accelerator to get more power.<P>Then I look up in my mirror to see what is going on behind me (traffic, etc.)  and what do I see?  Sparks.  Tons of sparks. So, I let off the gas and pull it out of gear and the sparks go away. Now, I'm thinking, "this is not good."<P>My biggest fear is that the thing is about to go up in flames.  I pull to the side of the road, and head back to the nearest gas station, call my wife and have a wrecker come get me and the Fiero and go home.<P><BR>A la Jerry Springer:<BR>Final thoughts.<BR>I am thinking that either my tranny blew, but no noise was heard, and the Fiero rolled fine during this incident, therefore I don't think that was it.<P>Or, I blew the engine - the most likely suspect, since I have been fighting oil leaks.  It is a distinct possibility that my oil pump stopped working and I began running metal to metal on the pistons and ceased the engine, hince the sparks flying through the exhaust.<P>Now, the two Fieros I had running are down, which means that every Fiero I own is non operational.  Talk about being in the dumps.<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-28-2001||10:36 AM||||aww man.  That does not sound good at all.  Did you happen to notice your oil pressure at all?  The oil light probably would have been screaming at you if the oil pump went out, wouldnt it?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||02-28-2001||01:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>aww man.  That does not sound good at all.  Did you happen to notice your oil pressure at all?  The oil light probably would have been screaming at you if the oil pump went out, wouldnt it?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know, I thought the same thing, but the gauges did not light up, until the car came to a complete stop.  Then, it's like, "thanks for nothin'!"<P>Everything seemed fine, then wham! nothing.  I have yet to dissect the Fiero, but I fear the worst.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||02-28-2001||01:54 PM||||How about this for crazy ?<P>You dropped your exhaust system, and when it hit the road, you got sparks and it bent the pipe shut...no flow, no power.<P>Hope that's it.||||reg||1
