Z||000007||Gold-86SE||03-01-2001||04:25 PM||||<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>How about this for crazy ?<P>You dropped your exhaust system, and when it hit the road, you got sparks and it bent the pipe shut...no flow, no power.<P>Hope that's it.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>deceler8, I wish.  Would have been a bunch cheaper than what I am looking at.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Wow that sounds cool sparks flying out the back. maybe people thought you had a low rider with hydro's sparking up the back. Oh and did you say you got passed by a geo metro?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Racer 1, I kinda wish I could have been one of the drivers behind me to see what it looked like, but my car in no way looks like a low rider.  And that metro, it went by so fast, I didn't recognize it as a metro - until my later and painful reflection up the pissy evening events.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Are you gonna try to fix that one or one of your other ones? That stinks, Hope you get a Fiero running soon<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>KRMFiero, well, here is what i am thinking.  Put my 86 back on the road, this weekend, hopefully.  Then fix the 85, then back to the 84, then the 87.  Sheesh, I have more work than one man should have.  Now, all I need is M O N E Y.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MoneypitGT||03-01-2001||07:00 PM||||When 3rd gear left my friends '87 GT the sparks and mild explosion was quite interesting so I heard. Most of the tranny came out of the bottom of the casing. The thing that sucked was the amount of oil all over EVERYTHING, it was especially bad when I had to pull it apart and put a new tranny in, after I bought it for $500.||||reg||2
